section: compiler
synopsis: Fix the RISC-V NCG sign-extending subword branch operands in place, corrupting live values
issues: #28050
mrs: !16998

description: {
  The signed subword path of ``genCondJump`` sign-extended its operands in
  place. If an operand was a local that remained live after the branch, its
  value was corrupted, violating the zero-extended subword invariant that the
  RISC-V NCG relies on.

  The operands are now sign-extended into fresh registers and the comparison is
  performed at 64-bit width, leaving the source registers untouched.
}
